  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Remove the periodic phases before taking the limit\n\nFor integer S,P, the periodic factor is constant on each pole ladder: eα = Exp[2 Pi I θα/h]. Replacing the two functionals (F1+F2, e1 F1+e2 F2) by (F1,F2) contributes exactly (e2-e1)^4 to the determinant. In the vacuum, remove Exp[(phi_i-phi_j) θα] from each ladder row; its product tends to one. The remaining entries are finite Laurent polynomials in z_i, since p=θα+n h. Thus a rational path z_i=1+eps psi_i permits an exact polynomial determinant calculation. Here h=1 as in prm; the leading phi differences equal eps(psi_i-psi_j), with no I bookkeeping factor.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[exVacMat, exVacLead, exPhase];\nexPhase = (Exp[2 Pi I (θ2/h /. prm)] - Exp[2 Pi I (θ1/h /. prm)])^4;\nexVacMat[S_, P_, ps_List] := Module[{rows, cols, zs = 1 + eps ps}, rows = Flatten[Table[{al, i, j}, {al, 2}, {i, 2}, {j, {4, 3}}], 2]; cols = Tuples[{{0, 1}, {0, 1}, {0, 1}}]; Outer[Function[{rr, cc}, With[{al = rr[[1]], i = rr[[2]], j = rr[[3]], sg = cc[[1]], tt = cc[[2]], be = cc[[3]]}, Together[Sum[With[{p = ({θ1, θ2}[[al]] + nn h) /. prm}, wE1[S, P, p] If[be == 0, 1, p] (zs[[i]]/zs[[j]])^nn zs[[j]]^-sg zs[[i]]^-tt], {nn, 0, {S, P}[[al]]}]]]], rows, cols, 1]];\nexVacLead[S_, P_, ps_List] := Module[{mat = exVacMat[S, P, ps], den, pol, dd, ord = 4 (S + P) + 8}, den = PolynomialLCM @@ (Denominator[Together[#]] & /@ #) & /@ mat; pol = MapThread[Cancel[#1 #2] &, {mat, den}]; dd = Factor[Det[pol]]; <|\"order\" -> Exponent[dd, eps, Min], \"coefficient\" -> Cancel[Coefficient[dd, eps, ord]/(Times @@ den /. eps -> 0)/cand[ps, {S + P, S + P, 0, 0}]], \"factored numerator\" -> dd|>];\nexV11 = exVacLead[1, 1, psiA];\n{exV11[\"order\"], exV11[\"coefficient\"], N[exPhase exV11[\"coefficient\"], 30], N[exPhase exV11[\"coefficient\"]/(vacLead/cand[psiA, {2, 2, 0, 0}]) - 1, 3]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
