   "value": "### Proven vacuum formula for arbitrary positive integer S,P\n\nSet L=S+P, t=(theta1-theta2)/h, eα=Exp[2 Pi I θα/h], and z_i=Exp[h phi_i]. For distinct simple pole ladders,\n\n$$N_{\\mathrm{vac}}=\\frac{(e_2-e_1)^4 h^{4-4L}}{\\left[S!P!\\prod_{k=-P}^{S}(t+k)\\right]^4}.$$\n\n**Proof.** Separate the two ladder functionals; their change of basis contributes (e2-e1)^4. Remove Exp[(phi_i-phi_j) θα] from each row (product tends to 1). Multiply ladder row (alpha,i,j) by z_i z_j^(Sα+1). The resulting polynomial matrix has entries\n\n`B[(alpha,i,j),(sigma,tau,beta)] = Sum[n=0..Sα] w(θα+n h) (θα+n h)^beta z_i^(n+1-tau) z_j^(Sα+1-n-sigma)`.\n\nIts determinant is homogeneous of degree 4L+8. When z1=z2 or z3=z4, four row pairs coincide, so the determinant contains (z1-z2)^4(z3-z4)^4. For each i in {1,2}, j in {3,4}, recombine the two ladder rows with the analytic factors Exp[(phi_i-phi_j) θα]. The full residue functional annihilates u^m for m<=L. Therefore beta=0 entries vanish to order L+1 and beta=1 entries to order L at z_i=z_j. This proves a factor (z_i-z_j)^L for each of the four cross pairs. These factors exhaust the degree: det B = K Delta(z), where Delta is exactly the vacuum twist prefactor in z.\n\nTo find K, take the highest powers z1^(2L+4) z2^(2L). Only tau=0 columns can go to the i=1 rows, tau=1 to i=2, and only n=Sα contributes. Each resulting 4x4 endpoint determinant is a tensor product of two 2x2 Vandermonde determinants. Hence\n\n`K=[(p2top-p1top) w(p1top) w(p2top)]^4 = h^(-8L-4)/[S! P! Product[t+k,{k,-P,S}]]^4`.\n\nAll row multipliers tend to 1 at confluence. Finally z_i-z_j = h(phi_i-phi_j)+higher orders, giving the displayed h^(4-4L) factor. This is a derivation for arbitrary integer spins, not an extrapolation from the four examples.\n\nThe exact finite-twist ladder determinant (before the removed exponentials) is\n\n`K Delta(z) / [(z1 z2)^4 (z3 z4)^(2L+4)]`.\n\nThe symbolic checks above cover (1,1), (2,1), (2,2), (3,1); further checks below include arbitrary twists.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[exD1OnShell];\nexD1OnShell[S_, P_, symbolic_: False] := Block[{prm = If[symbolic, {θ1 -> exT, θ2 -> 0, h -> 1}, prm]}, Module[{r0, rr, zz, mat, den, pol, dd, ray = {3, 0, 1, -3}, delta, lead}, r0 = (S P + P θ1 + S θ2)/(S + P) /. prm; rr = r0 + eps; delta = Cancel[-(S + P) eps/((rr - (θ1 /. prm)) (rr - (θ2 /. prm)))]; zz = 1 + delta ray; mat = Map[Cancel[Together[# /. eps -> delta]] &, exD1Mat[S, P, ray], {2}] /. exRoot -> rr; mat = Map[Cancel, mat, {2}]; den = PolynomialLCM @@ (Denominator[#] & /@ #) & /@ mat; pol = MapThread[Cancel[#1 #2] &, {mat, den}]; dd = Det[pol]; lead = Factor[Cancel[dd/(Times @@ den)/cand[zz, {S + P, S + P - 1, 1, 0}]]]; Factor[Limit[lead, eps -> 0]]]];\nexOn11 = TimeConstrained[exD1OnShell[1, 1, True], 40, $Aborted];\n{exOn11, If[exOn11 === $Aborted, \"symbolic on-shell determinant timed out\", Factor[exOn11/exVs11[\"coefficient\"]]]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
