  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Session 4 result and scope\n\nFor the balanced family mu={L-m,L-m,m,m}, d=2m, n=L-2m, define A=P1(theta1+S h) P1(theta2+P h) and B=Qbar12(theta1+S h) Qbar12(theta2+P h), all from the untwisted monic Q-functions.\n\n- **Proved for arbitrary spins:** d=2 has N/Nvac=8(L+1)^3(L+2) B^3/A^2; d=4 has N/Nvac=432(L-1)^3 L^4(L+1) B^3/A^2.\n- **Derived for all balanced even degrees:** `balancedQMat`/`balancedQNorm` gives an explicit 8x8 determinant entirely in the first two direct and dual untwisted Q-polynomials and finite residue sums. Its proof removes the common cross-pair zeros (phi_i-phi_j)^n before taking the four row confluent limits per functional. It does not require solving higher twisted corrections.\n- **Conjectured product for arbitrary m:** N/Nvac = m! (m+1)!^3 (n+3)_m^3 (n+4)_m B^3/A^2, with rising factorials. Proven at m=0,1,2; exact independent checks also pass at m=3 and m=4. The all-m product proof remains open.\n- **Not covered:** unbalanced irreps, including mu={L,L-2,2,0} at d=2 and mu={L-1,L-2,2,1} at d=3.\n\nThe explicit d=4 dependence is A_{-1}^3 A_0^4 A_1, where A_k=(S+k+t)(P+k-t). It disproves the extension of the earlier A_0^3 A_1 A_2 A_3 guess to this state.\n\nThe complete formulas, determinant definition, proof, verification table and limitations are in [N_untw_balanced_closed_form.md](N_untw_balanced_closed_form.md). The task briefing points to this result.\n\n**Minimal replay after a kernel restart:** run cells 2-5, 7, 12-13, 20, then 60, 62, 64-67. Confirm successful execution before advancing; a timeout is not proof that a dependency loaded. The remaining session-4 cells retain the independent exploratory and perturbative checks. The numeric helpers balEndpoint, balVacK, balQCandidate use h=1; balancedQMat and the written formula include general h.\n\nThe notebook was reopened after a VS Code restart on 2026-09-11; all 63 earlier cells were intact. The required kernel definitions were restored, the equal-weight d=4 identity rechecked, and the symbolic d=2,d=4 factorizations and d=6,d=8 checks were executed again or completed in the current live kernel.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Session 5: universal polynomial in the untwisted pairings\n\nUser target: one polynomial in the shifted bilinears <Pd_a u^beta P_i>_alpha, with coefficients independent of mu and preferably also S,P. All four direct and all four dual untwisted Q-functions are available. The balanced-family determinant has mu-dependent factorials and powers of u, so is not a solution to this stronger target.\n\nPlan: (1) construct the complete pairing tensor in the existing monic triangular gauge; (2) investigate its rank, gauge covariance and invariant degree-eight contractions against exact norms including unbalanced states; (3) derive and independently validate any candidate. No state-dependent coefficients may be hidden in the pairing definitions.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[univPairTensor, univCols, univFullRows];\nunivCols = Tuples[{{0, 1}, {0, 1}, {0, 1}}];\nunivFullRows = Tuples[{{1, 2}, Range[4], Range[4]}];\nunivPairTensor[ss_, pp_, mm_List] := Module[{pd = UntwSolve[ss, pp, mm][\"P\"], pl = UntwSolveD[ss, pp, mm][\"Pd\"], hh = h /. prm, pol, fn, xx}, Table[pol = Expand[u^col[[3]] qpoly[pd[[i]], u - col[[2]] hh] qpoly[pl[[a]], u + col[[1]] hh]]; If[al == 1, resSum[ss, pp, 1, pol], Total[Table[xx = (θ2 + kk hh) /. prm; wE1[ss, pp, xx] (pol /. u -> xx), {kk, 0, pp}]]], {al, 2}, {i, 4}, {a, 4}, {col, univCols}]];\nunivInitialStates = {{1,1,{2,2,0,0}},{1,1,{2,1,1,0}},{1,1,{1,1,1,1}},{2,1,{3,3,0,0}},{2,1,{3,2,1,0}},{2,1,{2,2,1,1}}};\nunivInitialTensors = (univPairTensor @@ # &) /@ univInitialStates;\nGrid[Prepend[MapThread[Function[{state,ten},{state,MatrixRank[Flatten[ten,2]],MatrixRank[Flatten[ten[[1]],1]],Table[Count[ten[[1,i,a]],Except[0]],{i,4},{a,4}]}],{univInitialStates,univInitialTensors}],{\"state\",\"full rank\",\"total-functional rank\",\"nonzero counts by (i,a)\"}],Frame->All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"51807\" data-output-id=\"12\" data-out-n=\"93\" data-sub-idx=\"6\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"69\" data-sub-start=\"6\" data-sub-end=\"6\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[93]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"7\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:30.0402em;vertical-align:-14.7501em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:15.2901em;\"><span style=\"top:-17.2501em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:17.2501em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:30.0002em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-14.7501em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:15.2501em;\"><span style=\"top:-19.0601em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.65em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">state</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-16.0501em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.65em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></s